Z||000046||fropuff||11-25-2000||06:06 PM||||Does anybody know what's going on?  I don't think I have much coolant left in the system; must have a busted hose or something.  Any ideas would be greatly appreciated.  Thanks a lot.||||reg||9
Z||000047||Seanh||11-25-2000||06:59 PM||||I would say to fill the cooling system, and then start and run the car in a driveway and check for leaks. If you find one, you have got your problem. Do you notice any white smoke from the tailpipes or under the decklid?||||reg||1
Z||000048||fropuff||11-25-2000||07:03 PM||||Nope, none coming from under the decklid.  There's a little smoke on startup, but it smells like exhaust and only lasts a minute or two.  I'll inspect for cracks in the hoses tomorrow.  What do you think caused this "overheat"?  Thanks a lot.||||reg||1
Z||000049||Joe4x4||11-25-2000||07:27 PM||||Did you check to see if your water pump is working?<BR>leave the stat cap off ( rear cap )<BR>start the fiero see if water is flowing .<P>I had little over heating problim last night . When I changed the antifreeze I did not tighten the the rear stat, and I was losing antifreeze.<P>good look. ||||reg||1
Z||000050||fropuff||11-25-2000||07:34 PM||||So I should add before I do all of this?  Because I have almost no coolant left in the system.  I'll check for leaks tomorrow, then I'll see if the water pump is working.  I think Fiero56 told me before that it could be this.  I thought it was working good, then it all screwed up.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000051||fropuff||02-25-2001||04:02 PM||||Okay, I ran the GT again just because I wanted to run all the fluids.  It ran for about 20 minutes, everything seemed okay.  All the same crap happened though.  The lines and everything got hot, but the oil pressure went down to around 25 psi.  It does go up when I rev the engine though.  I noticed that "steam" was coming from around the radiator once it heated up.  After all was done, I checked the oil.  There was no difference in smell or color, and there were no bubbles in it.  I don't know if I should do a compression test or not to check for something wrong with the head(s).  Should I?  Thanks.  As of now, I'm thinking the radiator, a clog in the system, water pump, ?  Thanks again.  I'm getting sick of this $hit.||||reg||1
Z||000052||sqoach||02-25-2001||10:56 PM||||i know the feeling. gets pretty damn aggravating. if you don't know if your water pump works or not, you better check that. did you check to see if the coolant is flowing with the stat cap off? another giveaway for the water pump to be shot is if you can see coolant coming out of the little holes on it. or if there is drops of coolant under your car. that's how i knew my pump went out. saw little coolant spots, then checked to see if coolant was coming out of the holes, which it was.<P>go ahead and do a compression check. couldn't hurt anything. also, get your water system pressure checked to see if there are any leaks. check both caps too. if the gasket is starting to go bad, it would allow air to get in there and screw everything up.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||12
Z||000053||fropuff||02-26-2001||04:01 PM||||Thanks for the help.  There is no coolant under the car, but I think something might be wrong with the thermostat cap, as a small amount of steam was coming out of the coolant tube through the cap.  I might get another one of those, as well as a non-vented 16 lb. radiator cap.  How do I go about doing a compression check?  What about the radiator?  There was quite a bit of steam coming out until I turned the fan on with the A/C.  Thanks again.||||reg||1
Z||000054||hugh||02-26-2001||06:12 PM||||I'm not real familiar with the control system for the fan,but on most cars the fan will come on when the air is turned because the condenser coil needs it.Under normal conditions the fan is controled by the temp switch on the engine.If the fan runs with the air and not with the engine it may be as simple as the switch on the engine. ||||reg||1
